---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { getRolls } from '../lib/rolls';

const rolls = await getRolls();
const frames = rolls.reduce((n, r) => n + r.data.exposures.length, 0);

const coffeeUrl = 'https://buymeacoffee.com/jesmith4evb';
---

<Base title="About" compact>
  <section class="about">
    <h1>Mostly out of focus</h1>
    <p>
      Jamm is the two of us — Samm and me — with a couple of old film cameras and
      not much idea what we're doing. We travel where we can, load a roll, and point
      the cameras at whatever the day puts in front of us.
    </p>
    <p>
      We are not good at this, and that turns out to be most of the fun. Exposures
      come back too dark or too bright, focus is a running argument with the lens,
      and every so often a whole frame is just black. We show each roll whole, in the
      order it was shot — the misses left in next to the few that landed.
    </p>
    <p>
      If any of it makes you smile, you can buy us a coffee. Leave a note with what we
      should spend it on — a real coffee, a cold beer, a pastry from wherever we've
      ended up — and we'll photograph it and slip it into a roll.
    </p>
    <a class="about__coffee" href={coffeeUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
      Buy us a coffee →
    </a>

    <dl class="colophon">
      <div>
        <dt>Rolls</dt>
        <dd>{rolls.length} archived</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Exposures</dt>
        <dd>{frames} frames</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Set in</dt>
        <dd>Space Grotesk &amp; Space Mono</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Built with</dt>
        <dd><a href="https://astro.build">Astro</a></dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Contact</dt>
        <dd><a href="mailto:hello@jamm.photography">hello@jamm.photography</a></dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </section>
</Base>
